:: Arcology Civic Boulevard
<<location "arcology_civic">><<run setup.arcology.visit("civic")>><<effects>>
<<arcologyDangerCheck "civic">><<if _arcologyDangerActive>><<exit>><</if>>
<<arcologySceneCheck "street">><<if _arcologyScene>><<include "Arcology Scene">><<exit>><</if>>
You are on Civic Boulevard, a broad avenue of white stone buildings with tall columns. The pavements are spotless, and security drones float above the road at regular intervals, each one turning to scan everyone who passes beneath it.
<br><br>
One turns towards you as you approach, following you with its scanner until you have walked past.
<br><br>
<<arcologyStreetHazards>>
<<if !_arcologyHalt>>
	Places of interest
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "registry">><<link [[Civic Registry (0:02)|Arcology Civic Registry]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "police">><<link [[Enforcement headquarters (0:02)|Arcology Enforcement]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "contracts">><<link [[Contract office (0:02)|Arcology Contract Office]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
	<br><br>
	<<arcologyStreets "civic">>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Civic Registry
<<location "arcology_registry">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
The registry hall is cold and mostly quiet. Small booths stand in rows, each marked with a number. Across from them, large screens cover the wall.
<br><br>
Near the entrance, you notice a screen showing what the registry offers. The registry can provide new implants, transfer personal records, and recover information from damaged chips.
<br><br>
<<if !$daily.arcologyRegistryCheck>>
	<<arcologyicon "record">><<link [[Check your record (0:15)|Arcology Civic Registry Record]]>><<set $daily.arcologyRegistryCheck to true>><<pass 15>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Civic Boulevard]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Civic Registry Record
<<location "arcology_registry">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
You take a number from the machine by the door and sit down to wait. When your number is called, you walk over to an empty booth. A small scanner is attached beside the screen.
<br><br>
You turn your head towards it, bringing the implant behind your ear to be scanned. A moment later, your personal information appears on the screen.
<br><br>
<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY / PUBLIC RECORD">>
	<<holoRow "HANDLE" `$xchange.arcology.handle or "UNREGISTERED"`>>
	<<holoRow "CLEARANCE" `($xchange.arcology.clearance or "guest").toUpperCase()`>>
	<<holoRow "SPONSOR" `$xchange.arcology.guest.sponsor ? $xchange.arcology.guest.sponsor.toUpperCase() : "NONE"`>>
	<<holoRow "RECORD READS" `($xchange.arcology.recognizable or 0) + " LOGGED"`>>
	<<holoLine "RECORD BACKUP NOT AVAILABLE FOR GUESTS" "warn">>
<</holo>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Civic Registry]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Enforcement
<<location "arcology_enforcement">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
The entrance hall of the enforcement headquarters has walls covered in black glass. Officers wearing grey armour walk through the hall without stopping.
<br><br>
Behind a high desk, a sergeant is reading from an implant screen. The sergeant's eyes move along lines of text that you can't see.
<br><br>
A large screen above the desk shows a list of people who have recently been arrested. Only their usernames are shown, with one of three words next to each name: <i>fined</i>, <i>transferred</i>, or <i>erased</i>.
The screen gives no explanation of what <i>erased</i> means.
<br><br>
<<if !$daily.arcologyEnforcementAsk>>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask for help (0:05)|Arcology Enforcement Ask]]>><<set $daily.arcologyEnforcementAsk to true>><<pass 5>><<arcologyNPC 0 "staff" "sergeant">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Civic Boulevard]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Enforcement Ask
<<location "arcology_enforcement">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<person1>>
You walk up to the counter and start asking what Enforcement can do for a visitor who runs into trouble. Behind the desk is a <<person>> wearing a grey visor pushed up onto <<his>> forehead. <<arcologyCyberLook 0>> Before you can finish speaking, <<he>> checks your implant and interrupts you.
<br><br>
"You're registered as a guest," <<he>> says. "We're here to protect residents. If you have a sponsor, keeping you safe is your sponsor's job. If you don't have a sponsor, you'll have to look after yourself."
<br><br>
<<He>> points towards the door. "Stay on the streets with lights, and don't let strangers get too close to your ear."
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Arcology Enforcement]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Contract Office
<<location "arcology_contracts">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
The contract office looks more like a travel agency, with comfortable chairs and pictures of the sea on the walls. A large screen displays a list of jobs available around the city. Each job shows how much it pays, where it takes place, and what kind of work is required: <i>escort</i>, <i>recovery</i>, or <i>removal</i>.
<br><br>
Several people are waiting in the chairs, although they don't look like ordinary customers. Most of them are carrying weapons, while others have mechanical arms or other metal parts replacing large sections of their bodies.
<br><br>
You walk closer to the screen, hoping to find out more about the jobs. However, when you try to read the details, the words become blurry, making them impossible to read. Before you can do anything else, a warning appears in front of your eyes:
<br><br>
<span class="blue">CONTRACTS ARE OFFERED TO REGISTERED OPERATORS ONLY.</span>
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Civic Boulevard]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Medtech Street
<<location "arcology_medtech">><<run setup.arcology.visit("medtech")>><<effects>>
<<arcologyDangerCheck "medtech">><<if _arcologyDangerActive>><<exit>><</if>>
<<arcologySceneCheck "street">><<if _arcologyScene>><<include "Arcology Scene">><<exit>><</if>>
You are on Medtech Street. Clinics and shops offering changes to people's faces and bodies stand on both sides of the road. Large screens in their windows advertise different treatments.
<br><br>
<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	Most of the clinics are closed for the night. The shops offering body changes are still open, with bright advertisements shining through their windows and onto the pavement.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<arcologyStreetHazards>>
<<if !_arcologyHalt>>
	Places of interest
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "clinic">><<link [[Lumen Clinic (0:01)|Arcology Lumen Clinic]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "augment">><<link [[Second Skin (0:01)|Arcology Second Skin]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br><br>
	<<arcologyStreets "medtech">>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Lumen Clinic
<<location "arcology_clinic">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
Lumen Clinic has clean white walls and a strong smell of disinfectant. At the front desk, a receptionist checks your implant and explains which treatments are available to guests. The prices appear on a screen, but the other treatments are locked.
<br><br>
<<if $daily.arcologyClinic>>
	<span class="blue">You've already received treatment today.</span>
	<br>
<<elseif $pain lt 20 and $stress lt $stressmax / 2>>
	The receptionist checks your condition and tells you that you <span class="blue">don't need treatment right now.</span>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<<set _lcP to setup.arcologyPrice.quote("treatment")>>
	<<if setup.arcologyPrice.affordable(_lcP)>>
		<span class="arc-priced"><<arcologyicon "clinic">><<link `"Treatment (" + _lcP.label + ", 0:30)"` "Arcology Lumen Treatment">><<if setup.arcologyPrice.pay("treatment")>><<set $daily.arcologyClinic to true>><<pass 30>><<pain -20>><<stress -6>><<else>><<set $phase to "unpaid">><</if>><</link>></span><<lllpain>><<lstress>>
	<<else>>
		<span class="blue">You need <<print _lcP.label>> to receive treatment.</span>
	<</if>>
	<<arcologyPriceNote _lcP>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Medtech Street]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Lumen Treatment
<<location "arcology_clinic">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<if $phase is "unpaid">>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	The receptionist looks at the payment screen and asks you to wait. The treatment wasn't paid for, so nobody calls you through.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Lumen Clinic]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
A nurse leads you into a small treatment room and asks you to sit in a chair beside a medical screen. After checking your health information, the nurse takes a cable from the machine and connects it to the implant behind your ear.
"Keep your head still, please."
<br><br>
You then feel something cool spreading from the back of your neck into the rest of your body. As the treatment continues, your muscles slowly relax, and the pain you were feeling begins to disappear. The nurse watches the screen for a little longer before disconnecting the cable.
<br><br>
"Your implant tells us when you're in pain. That way, we know what needs treating without having to ask you."
The nurse puts the cable away before adding, "Some patients don't like us having access to that information. They complain about it at first, but strangely, they never bring it up again."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Lumen Clinic]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Second Skin
<<location "arcology_augment">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
Second Skin is a shop that sells artificial body parts. Purple lights fill the room, with soft velvet chairs placed near the walls.
<br><br>
The owner sits behind the counter, watching you as you look around the shop. On a stand by the counter, a hand made of clear glass catches the light. You pick it up and turn it over, curious about how the fingers are connected. The owner notices what you're doing but makes no attempt to stop you.
<br><br>
"Visitors can look, but only residents can buy," the owner says.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Medtech Street]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Signal Avenue
<<location "arcology_signal">><<run setup.arcology.visit("signal")>><<effects>>
<<arcologyDangerCheck "signal">><<if _arcologyDangerActive>><<exit>><</if>>
<<arcologySceneCheck "street">><<if _arcologyScene>><<include "Arcology Scene">><<exit>><</if>>
You are on Signal Avenue. Almost every building has antennas on its roof, with thick cables hanging above the street to connect them. Large screens on the buildings show the latest news, while people walk past on their way to work or stop briefly to watch.
<br><br>
<<arcologyStreetHazards>>
<<if !_arcologyHalt>>
	Places of interest
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "news">><<link [[Dome Broadcast (0:02)|Arcology Dome Broadcast]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "terminal">><<link [[Public terminals (0:01)|Arcology Terminals]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "intel">><<link [[Grey building (0:02)|Arcology Intelligence Division]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
	<br><br>
	<<arcologyStreets "signal">>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Dome Broadcast
<<location "arcology_broadcast">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
The Dome Broadcast lobby is filled with large screens showing different news channels. Visitors walk around the room, stopping to watch stories that interest them.
<br><br>
<<set _dbNews to setup.arcologyNews.feed()>>
<<if _dbNews.length>>
	The largest screen shows today's top story: <i><<print _dbNews[0].title>></i>.
	<<if _dbNews[1]>>A ticker below it scrolls through the next one: <i><<print _dbNews[1].title>></i>.<</if>>
<<else>>
	The screens show the Dome Broadcast logo while the next bulletin loads.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link "Read the news wall">><<run setup.arcologyNews.mode = "lobby">><<replace "#domeNews">><<arcologyNewsReader>><</replace>><</link>>
<div id="domeNews"></div>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Signal Avenue]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Terminals
<<location "arcology_signal">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
Several public computers stand under a small shelter at the side of the avenue. Each screen asks to scan your implant before you can use the computer.
<br><br>
<<if !$daily.arcologyTerminal>>
	<<arcologyicon "terminal">><<link [[Read the public feeds (0:10)|Arcology Terminals Feed]]>><<set $daily.arcologyTerminal to true>><<pass 10>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<arcologyicon "search">><<link [[Search for your handle (0:05)|Arcology Terminals Search]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Signal Avenue]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Terminals Feed
<<location "arcology_signal">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
You scroll through the public posts. Most of them are adverts for shops and services, but you also find a few notices mixed in.
<br><br>
<<holoNotice "REGISTRY WARNING" "If your identity chip is damaged while trying to copy it without permission, the Registry will not repair it." "warn">>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Terminals]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Terminals Search
<<location "arcology_signal">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _exposure to $xchange.arcology.recognizable or 0>>
You type your handle into the search bar.
<br><br>
<<if _exposure lte 0>>
	<<holoNotice "PUBLIC FEEDS" "NO RESULTS. YOUR HANDLE HAS NOT BEEN MENTIONED." "ok">>
<<elseif _exposure lte 2>>
	<<holoNotice "PUBLIC FEEDS" "A FEW MENTIONS. SOMEONE HAS ASKED ABOUT YOUR OLD IDENTITY." "warn">>
<<else>>
	<<holoNotice "PUBLIC FEEDS" "MANY MENTIONS. YOUR RECORD IS BEING TRADED." "denied">>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Terminals]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Intelligence Division
<<location "arcology_intel">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
At the end of Signal Avenue, you find a grey building with no windows or signs to tell you what it is. The front door is closed, and you can't see any handle, button or scanner that would let you open it.
<br><br>
You walk up to the door and look around for a way inside. Before you can do anything, a warning suddenly appears in front of your eyes.
<br><br>
<<holoNotice "UNLISTED" "VISITOR LOGGED. YOU HAVE NO BUSINESS HERE." "denied">>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Signal Avenue]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>
